/data/*
!/data/mvp_masterplan.md

# Tooling caches (minimal P3 entries; full .gitignore pass is P4)
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# M3-P2 /export importer quarantine sidecars (never commit; may reference
# engine-minted source ids). Configurable path via --quarantine-report.
*.quarantine.json

# Parity-suite run output (A1-P1). The committed baselines live in
# app/tests/__baselines__/ and are tracked; these are per-run artifacts only.
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/

# Workflow artifacts downloaded from CI runs (debug APKs, reports, scorecards).
# Build outputs of a run, never sources; from the release-signing milestone the
# same directory also receives signed release binaries.
ci-artifacts/

# Signing material, repository-wide (RSN-CLOSE). The release key lives in
# Actions secrets and is never in the tree — but the ignore coverage was uneven
# (native/android/ knew about PKCS12, native/ knew only .jks/.keystore, and this
# file knew nothing), and the failure mode of that gap is a private key in git
# history, which no later commit removes. Handling keystore material outside
# this tree is still the rule; this is the net under it.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pfx

# Standard ignores (P4 pass)
.venv/
__pycache__/
node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/
htmlcov/
.cache/
.tox/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store
*.log
.env*
!.env.example

# Graph artifacts (ADR-049). Generated by the vault graph tooling — a report and
# the data behind it, regenerated on demand and never a source. Unanchored on
# purpose: they stay ignored wherever the generator's working directory lands.
graph.json
graph.html
GRAPH_REPORT.md
